## 9. Mean imputation in the involvement scales
The scales have 3 items (inv_app, inv_dl) and 8 items (inv_cat) on a 1-7
range, so the scale means must be multiples of 1/3 and 1/8. A value that is
not, and that equals the scale mean, is the signature of mean imputation.

  inv_app  (3 items) mean = 5.328532 | attainable score on the scale? NO  | cases equal to the mean:  5 (1.0%)
           s.d. including = 1.0533 | s.d. excluding = 1.0587 | difference = +0.0054
  inv_dl   (3 items) mean = 4.693306 | attainable score on the scale? NO  | cases equal to the mean:  3 (0.6%)
           s.d. including = 1.2987 | s.d. excluding = 1.3027 | difference = +0.0040
  inv_cat  (8 items) mean = 4.480208 | attainable score on the scale? NO  | cases equal to the mean: 11 (2.2%)
           s.d. including = 1.0640 | s.d. excluding = 1.0762 | difference = +0.0121

  subjects with at least one imputed scale: 18 of 491 (3.7%)
