## 12. What the 'manipulation check' actually is (questionnaire slide 6)
It is not a check that the manipulation was perceived. It is a single
multiple-choice question asked once at the end ('which factors did you take
into consideration'), with 9 tick boxes. man_check_i = 1 if the matching box
was ticked. Two consequences are visible in the data:

  (a) it is a compositional measure: ticking one box comes at the expense of others.
      Correlations between the three outcomes within subject:
                  man_check_i.rep man_check_i.pop man_check_i.brand
man_check_i.rep             1.000           0.305            -0.067
man_check_i.pop             0.305           1.000            -0.091
man_check_i.brand          -0.067          -0.091             1.000
      An attention measure would show uniformly positive correlations.

  (b) being a single global question, it cannot vary by presentation position:
        check
position     0     1
       1 0.316 0.684
       2 0.308 0.692
       3 0.326 0.674
      That flatness is structural, not evidence against memory decay.
